      "value": "@{58c62e995865713647a7115b|full_name}: I just tried this out and from what I can tell, it seems to be \"mostly\" fixed.  It seems the core functionality is working, however, there's an issue with the name of the world that is displayed.  \n\nIf I upload an update to a world I'm in, I can see the name of the newest version of the world.  When I click on it, however, it opens up with a detailed view of the old version of the world.  At least, it shows the name of the previous (old) version.  If I drop a portal, the name on the portal, from my perspective, is the name the old version, but to anyone accompanying me, they see the name of the new version.  Regardless, when we both jump in, we are taken the newest version.\n\nTo summarize, yes, the core functionality is working, but the incorrect world names popping up in the worlds menu is confusing and does not correctly display the name of the world you are about to go/drop a portal in to.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
